 The oracle is `__real_to_text`, `codex/compiler/Emit/X86_64TextHelpers.codex:590`,
 and the FORMAT is the part that has to match rather than the arithmetic: at most
 fifteen fractional digits, trailing zeros stripped down to one, always a dot and
 always a digit after it. The two diverge above 2^63, where `cvttsd2si` answers
 the integer indefinite and `i64.trunc_sat_f64_s` saturates; no `.expected` in the
 corpus spells a value that large.

