 Text here is a pointer to `[i32 length][bytes]` and a list is a pointer to
 `[i32 count][i32 capacity][i64 elements]`, both from `$bump_alloc`. The
 digits and the minus sign are ASCII, 48 and 45, which is what `$i64_to_text`
 writes on the way out.

 `$cx_text_match_at` is the one primitive the other four need: whether `sub`
 occurs in `s` at a byte offset. An EMPTY sub matches everywhere, which is
 what makes contains answer True and starts-with answer True for one, as the
 foreword definitions do.

 The cell layout and the reversing fill are x86-64's, not a choice made here:
 `emit-linked-list-push-builtin` (`X86_64Builtins.codex`) conses a 16-byte
 `[value][next]` onto the FRONT, and `emit-linked-list-to-list-helper`
 (`X86_64Helpers.codex`) walks that chain filling the result back to front.
 An append-at-tail list answers every length and membership question
 identically and hands back every sequence backwards.

  wat-rt-linked-list : Text =
   "  (func $ll_push (param $lst i64) (param $val i64) (result i64)\n" &
   "    (local $p i32)\n" &
   "    (local.set $p (call $bump_alloc (i32.const 16)))\n" &
   "    (i64.store (local.get $p) (local.get $val))\n" &
   "    (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.const 8)) (local.get $lst))\n" &
   "    (i64.extend_i32_u (local.get $p)))\n\n" &
   "  (func $ll_to_list (param $head i64) (result i64)\n" &
   "    (local $cur i32) (local $n i32) (local $dst i32) (local $i i32)\n" &
   "    (local.set $cur (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $head)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $n (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (block $lcd (loop $lcl\n" &
   "      (br_if $lcd (i32.eqz (local.get $cur)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $n (i32.add (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $cur (i32.wrap_i64 (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $cur) (i32.const 8)))))\n" &
   "      (br $lcl)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $dst (call $bump_alloc (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $n) (i32.const 8)))))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (local.get $dst) (local.get $n))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.const 4)) (local.get $n))\n" &
   "    (local.set $cur (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $head)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $i (local.get $n))\n" &
   "    (block $lfd (loop $lfl\n" &
   "      (br_if $lfd (i32.eqz (local.get $cur)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $i (i32.sub (local.get $i) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "      (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $i) (i32.const 8))))\n" &
   "        (i64.load (local.get $cur)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $cur (i32.wrap_i64 (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $cur) (i32.const 8)))))\n" &
   "      (br $lfl)))\n" &
   "    (i64.extend_i32_u (local.get $dst)))\n\n" &
   "  (func $text_concat_list (param $lst i64) (result i64)\n" &
   "    (local $p i32) (local $n i32) (local $i i32) (local $total i32)\n" &
   "    (local $dst i32) (local $at i32) (local $e i32) (local $el i32) (local $k i32)\n" &
   "    (local.set $p (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $lst)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $n (i32.load (local.get $p)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $p (call $cx_list_base (local.get $lst)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $total (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (local.set $i (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (block $tsd (loop $tsl\n" &
   "      (br_if $tsd (i32.ge_s (local.get $i) (local.get $n)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $total (i32.add (local.get $total)\n" &
   "        (i32.load (i32.wrap_i64 (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $i) (i32.const 8)))))))))\n" &
   "      (local.set $i (i32.add (local.get $i) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "      (br $tsl)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $dst (call $bump_alloc (i32.add (local.get $total) (i32.const 4))))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (local.get $dst) (local.get $total))\n" &
   "    (local.set $at (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.const 4)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $i (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (block $tcd (loop $tcl\n" &
   "      (br_if $tcd (i32.ge_s (local.get $i) (local.get $n)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $e (i32.wrap_i64 (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $i) (i32.const 8)))))))\n" &
   "      (local.set $el (i32.load (local.get $e)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $k (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "      (block $tbd (loop $tbl\n" &
   "        (br_if $tbd (i32.ge_s (local.get $k) (local.get $el)))\n" &
   "        (i32.store8 (i32.add (local.get $at) (local.get $k))\n" &
   "          (i32.load8_u (i32.add (i32.add (local.get $e) (i32.const 4)) (local.get $k))))\n" &
   "        (local.set $k (i32.add (local.get $k) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "        (br $tbl)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $at (i32.add (local.get $at) (local.get $el)))\n" &
   "      (local.set $i (i32.add (local.get $i) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "      (br $tcl)))\n" &
   "    (i64.extend_i32_u (local.get $dst)))\n\n"

 `list-insert-at` takes `0 <= i <= len`, one looser than `list-at` at the top
 end: inserting AT the length is an append. Out of range is `unreachable`,
 which is `ud2` on x86-64 (`X86_64ListHelpers.codex` Section
 `__list_insert_at`); this quire's first standing hazard is that emitting
 something plausible for a case we cannot serve is worse than refusing.

 It fills in place when the capacity allows, as x86-64 and `$list_push` both
 do. Always copying would be simpler and would make n inserts cost O(n^2) on
 an allocator that never frees, which is the pairing `__list-with-capacity`
 exists to avoid.

  wat-rt-list-insert : Text =
   "  (func $list_with_capacity (param $cap i64) (result i64)\n" &
   "    (local $c i32) (local $dst i32)\n" &
   "    (local.set $c (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $cap)))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.lt_s (local.get $c) (i32.const 0)) (then (local.set $c (i32.const 0))))\n" &
   "    (local.set $dst (call $bump_alloc (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $c) (i32.const 8)))))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (local.get $dst) (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.const 4)) (local.get $c))\n" &
   "    (i64.extend_i32_u (local.get $dst)))\n\n" &
   "  (func $list_insert_at (param $lst i64) (param $idx i64) (param $val i64) (result i64)\n" &
   "    (local $p i32) (local $n i32) (local $cap i32) (local $i i32) (local $dst i32) (local $k i32) (local $nc i32)\n" &
   "    (local.set $p (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $lst)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $n (i32.load (local.get $p)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $cap (i32.load (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.const 4))))\n" &
   "    (local.set $p (call $cx_list_base (local.get $lst)))\n" &
   "    (local.set $i (i32.wrap_i64 (local.get $idx)))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.lt_s (local.get $i) (i32.const 0)) (then (unreachable)))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.gt_s (local.get $i) (local.get $n)) (then (unreachable)))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.lt_s (local.get $n) (local.get $cap))\n" &
   "      (then\n" &
   "        (local.set $k (i32.sub (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "        (block $isd (loop $isl\n" &
   "          (br_if $isd (i32.lt_s (local.get $k) (local.get $i)))\n" &
   "          (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 16) (i32.mul (local.get $k) (i32.const 8))))\n" &
   "            (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $k) (i32.const 8))))))\n" &
   "          (local.set $k (i32.sub (local.get $k) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "          (br $isl)))\n" &
   "        (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $i) (i32.const 8)))) (local.get $val))\n" &
   "        (i32.store (local.get $p) (i32.add (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "        (return (i64.extend_i32_u (local.get $p)))))\n" &
   "    (local.set $nc (i32.mul (local.get $cap) (i32.const 2)))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.lt_s (local.get $nc) (i32.add (local.get $n) (i32.const 1))) (then (local.set $nc (i32.add (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))))\n" &
   "    (if (i32.lt_s (local.get $nc) (i32.const 4)) (then (local.set $nc (i32.const 4))))\n" &
   "    (local.set $dst (call $bump_alloc (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $nc) (i32.const 8)))))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (local.get $dst) (i32.add (local.get $n) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "    (i32.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.const 4)) (local.get $nc))\n" &
   "    (local.set $k (i32.const 0))\n" &
   "    (block $iad (loop $ial\n" &
   "      (br_if $iad (i32.ge_s (local.get $k) (local.get $i)))\n" &
   "      (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $k) (i32.const 8))))\n" &
   "        (i64.load (i32.add (local.get $p) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $k) (i32.const 8))))))\n" &
   "      (local.set $k (i32.add (local.get $k) (i32.const 1)))\n" &
   "      (br $ial)))\n" &
   "    (i64.store (i32.add (local.get $dst) (i32.add (i32.const 8) (i32.mul (local.get $i) (i32.const 8)))) (local.get $val))\n" &
   "    (local.set $k (local.get $i))\n" &
